      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I went and Debugged this with ぐらりぃる over at discord and Figured out that if one is using UnityHub via flatpak you MUST have to point to the flatpak directory instead of .local/share\n\nFor Example \n\nln -s ~/.local/share/Steam/steamapps/compatdata/438100/pfx/drive_c/users/steamuser/AppData/LocalLow/VRChat ~/.var/app/com.unity.UnityHub/data/VRChat\n\nThe SDK should take the various different directories to account where linux may be throwing these and allow us to point directly to where VRC is installed instead.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
